# Build output
/preflight
/preflight.exe
/bin/
/dist/

# Go
*.test
*.exe
*.out
coverage.*

# Terraform working files. Plans and state can contain infrastructure detail
# that should never end up in a public repo.
*.tfplan
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
# ...except for derivation fixtures. A derived action set is only valid for the
# provider version that produced it, and the lock file is what pins that. Without
# it committed, re-running a derivation silently uses whatever provider is
# current, and a behaviour change would be recorded against a version nobody ran.
!derivefixtures/**/.terraform.lock.hcl
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Real plan output captured while testing against live infrastructure.
# Fixtures under testdata/ are deliberately re-included below.
plan.json
*.plan.json

# Contract-test fixture outputs — contain real account IDs and role ARNs
testfixtures/aws/fixtures.json

# Credentials
.env
.envrc
*.pem
credentials
.claude

# Documentation.
#
# The engineering documents SHIP, as of 2026-09-25. They were excluded while
# this was a private scratchpad, which meant a clone carried no CLAUDE.md, no
# schema reference and no contributor guide — fine for one machine, wrong for a
# codebase other people and other agents are meant to maintain. The mapping
# database is explicitly a community asset (SPECS §8); a contributor cannot
# promote an entry without the standard that says how.
#
# GENERAL_DIRECTION.md stays out. It is strategy, business model, competitive
# positioning and exit context — working material for the founders, not part of
# the product.
*.md
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/SPECS.md
!docs/**/*.md
!mappings/**/*.md
!testfixtures/**/*.md
!derivefixtures/**/*.md

# Test fixtures are checked in on purpose
!**/testdata/**

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
